<title>HUNGARY: Hungarian finmin says Posta Bank &quot;solvent&quot;.</title>
<headline>Hungarian finmin says Posta Bank &quot;solvent&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungarian Finance Minister Peter Medgyessy said on Friday that the country's third largest bank, Posta Bank, hit by a run by depositors, is solvent.</p>
<p>&quot;The Posta Bank is solvent and liquid and it is only a rumour that was spread about the financial institution,&quot; Medgyessy told the Hungarian news agency MTI after the run on the bank thousands of depositors.</p>
<p>The finance ministry was due to hold a news conference later in the day, MTI reported.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom ++ 36 327 4041</p>
</text>
